nodecode-roam is a rewrite of vcruz305's vcruz305/hermes-roam:

  https://github.com/vcruz305/hermes-roam
  commit 8b9fba41fea77f2fe2d6d572cffd43039d2da11f
  Apache-2.0, Copyright (c) 2026 Victor Cruz (LICENSE)

The rewritten plugin is the repository at that commit. What it does for a
person is what this cell does: one sealed bundle of the home in storage they
own, pushed from one machine and restored onto another, looked at first and
restored second, with the model able to look and push while the restore that
writes stays the operator's. The three tools keep the original's names --
roam_status, roam_push, roam_pull -- and its answers keep the same members
(success, message, version, files, bytes, applied, the per-file plan), and
the original's /roam command is a Nodecode slash command of that name. Its
discipline is kept as well: AES-256-GCM with a random nonce, a head signed
with an HKDF subkey and used as the AEAD's associated data so an edited store
fails authentication, one digest of the contents for comparing two machines,
a push refused when the store moved past what this home last saw, a restore
planned before it writes, every replaced file backed up under .roam/backups/
with a journal, a path outside the home refused, and allow_agent_apply off by
default so the model cannot write files on its own.

What was rewritten, and how: the engine is Common Lisp against the Nodecode
cell contract instead of Python against the Hermes plugin API. The original's
tar archive became one file of this cell's own format -- magic, head, meta,
sealed body -- so a reader needs no tar and no pickle; the scope is one
declared include/exclude list over the Nodecode home instead of the
original's shared and local profile slices; and the state that used to be
Hermes's own bookkeeping (last version, last digest, when it last pushed) is
one small JSON file under .roam/. The passphrase is read from an environment
variable or a file the section names, never from the config itself.

What was left out, and why: the S3 signer and the git backend. A cell may
reach HTTP and the CLI the user has, and should not carry SigV4 for one
vendor; a presigned S3 or R2 URL, a WebDAV endpoint or a signing proxy gives
the same store over the one HTTPS path, and a git repository is a folder that
git already syncs. The cron-installed scheduled push, the pre-LLM hook that
looked for a newer remote, and the bundled setup skill are the section and
the primer now: Nodecode's own /settings and (help :roam) carry what the
skill used to say, and a push is a tool call or a shift between two
machines rather than a timer.
